# Operation contract

Pokerlost business APIs use one private JSON operation protocol over HTTPS.

## Operations and paths

Every business operation matches:

```text
operation_id = lowerCamelCase verb name
path         = "/" + operation_id
HTTP method  = POST
```

The exact identifier pattern is `^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*$`. Valid examples include `getMe`,
`registerAccount`, and `provisionHuman`. Dots, underscores, hyphens, and uppercase initials are
invalid. The generator validates all source documents together and rejects global operation or
schema collisions before writing.

`GET /`, `GET /getOpenApi`, and existing health probes are public bodyless infrastructure
exceptions. Business GET bodies and other business HTTP methods are unsupported.

Each static router is one flat module with a module-level `router = APIRouter(...)` and
module-level decorated endpoints. Do not use router factories, nested endpoint functions, nested
router directories, imperative registration, one-use route constants, or post-hoc mutation.

## Requests

Every business operation accepts `PokerlostRequest[Payload]`:

```json
{
  "payload": {
    "username": "alice"
  }
}
```

Payload types are named closed Pydantic models with snake_case wire fields. Typed fields and focused
Pydantic validators own primitive parsing and cross-field wire invariants; routes do not parse UUIDs,
enums, audiences, or other primitive inputs. Requests do not use business path/query parameters,
cookies, form data, caller-supplied transport metadata, embedded anonymous bodies, or manual content
negotiation.

Protected operations additionally require `Authorization: Bearer <access-token>`. Authentication
never appears in the JSON body. See `docs/api/header-authorization.md`.

## Responses

Every business success and handled failure uses `PokerlostResponse`. A normal route declares the
typed envelope as `response_model` and returns plain data for FastAPI validation/serialization.
Only centralized exception/error handling manually builds `PokerlostResponse[None]` and
`JSONResponse`. The five-field invariant is documented in `docs/api/pokerlost-response.md`.

## Scopes

Scope IDs are separate from operation IDs. Protected routes declare exact non-empty values through
FastAPI `Security`; standard OpenAPI carries those values into the generated SDK method's explicit
`__scopes__` tuple. A method without access-token security declares `__scopes__ is None`; an empty
tuple is invalid.
